I think redefining the meaning of sectioning commands would create considerable
confusion in LaTeX3.

Maybe one should just have something like
	\chapter equivalent  to \Section{0}
	etc.

The (in my opinion) nicest way of inserting a section tree somewhere
in a document would be via an environment that defines an offset to
the section depth, s.th. like:
	\begin{sectree}
		\Section{0}{...}
			\Section{1}{...}
	\end{sectree}
